hadamardPower(Ideal,ZZ) -- computes the $r$-th Hadmard powers of varieties
**************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hadamardPower: hadamardPower,
  * Usage: 
        hadamardPower(I,r)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of *note (homogeneous) ideals:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a positive integer $>=1$
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

Give a homogeneous ideal $I$, the $r$-th Hadamard power of $I$ is $r$-times
Hadamard product of I to itself; $( I x\cdots x I)_{r-times}$

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x,y,z,w]                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=ideal(random(1,S),random(1,S),random(1,S))                            |
|                                                                             |
|            9    9    3    7   7     7     7    7        3    6              |
|o2 = ideal (-x + -y + -z + -w, -x + --y + --z + -w, 7x + -y + -z + 6w)       |
|            2    4    4    4   9    10    10    3        7    7              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : hadamardPower(I,3)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = ideal (714516984z + 60190200559w, 714516984y - 2454911549w, 26463592x + |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     1860867w)                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

