Point -- a new type for points in projective space
**************************************************

Description
===========

A point in projective space is represented as an object in the class *note
Point: Point,. An element of this class is a *note BasicList:
(Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,.

Methods that use an object of class Point:
==========================================

  * *note Point * Point: Point _st Point, -- entrywise product of two
    projective points
  * *note Point == Point: Point == Point, -- check equality of two projective
    points

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Point: Point, is a *note type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with
ancestor classes *note BasicList: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList, < *note Thing:
(Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

